# Git LFS tracking.
#
# Scoped to three exact paths, never `data/optical/*.fits`. The other 39 frames
# are already in this repository's history as plain git objects: a wildcard
# would not shrink the clone, and it would rewrite how every existing checkout
# resolves them. Keep this list explicit, one path per frame, the way
# .gitleaks.toml's allowlist is path-scoped for the same reason.
#
# These three are here because each carries four Afterglow-aligned exposures at
# 31 MB, well over the 9 MB cut-off that governs what data/optical/ puts in
# plain git (data/README.md). Fetch them with `git lfs install && git lfs pull`;
# without them the suite skips the tests that need the pixels.
data/optical/ngc5286_globular_b_000.fits filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
data/optical/ngc5286_globular_b_001.fits filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
data/optical/ngc5286_globular_b_002.fits filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
